    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "But you basically just said income-based is the best one for \"true equity.\" If we go with a lottery, we're just playing a game of chance with people's lives, which feels inherently unfair to the people who are struggling most. Isn't it just a fact that any system that doesn't prioritize the poorest residents first is failing the equity test?",
